WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:05.811
A hunt plan records the hypothesis, rationale, scope, time range, assets, data sources,

00:00:05.811 --> 00:00:09.325
expected behavior, reviewers, safety constraints, and completion criteria.

00:00:09.325 --> 00:00:15.475
This structure makes the work repeatable and prevents the investigation from expanding without purpose.

00:00:15.475 --> 00:00:20.307
Preserve evidence references, searches, observations, and decisions as the hunt progresses.

00:00:20.307 --> 00:00:25.579
Findings should distinguish facts from interpretation and assign a confidence level based

00:00:25.579 --> 00:00:27.775
on coverage and source quality.

00:00:27.775 --> 00:00:33.486
Record disconfirming evidence and unresolved gaps, not only observations that fit the theory.

00:00:33.486 --> 00:00:37.439
Escalation paths should identify security, operations, engineering, site leadership,

00:00:37.439 --> 00:00:38.757
and incident-response contacts.

00:00:38.757 --> 00:00:41.393
High-consequence findings may require rapid coordination,

00:00:41.393 --> 00:00:44.029
but response authority should remain clear.

00:00:44.029 --> 00:00:47.982
Documentation helps teams act without improvising around sensitive systems.

00:00:47.982 --> 00:00:49.300
Operationalize repeatable findings.

00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:54.571
A reliable pattern may become a detection, dashboard, watchlist, or recurring review.

00:00:54.571 --> 00:00:58.525
Document required fields, thresholds, exclusions, asset context, investigation steps,

00:00:58.525 --> 00:01:03.796
and ownership so the output can be maintained after the original hunt.

00:01:03.796 --> 00:01:05.993
Hunts also improve foundational data.

00:01:05.993 --> 00:01:10.386
Update asset inventory when new systems or dependencies are validated.

00:01:10.386 --> 00:01:15.218
Record blind spots, repair collection gaps, improve time and identity mapping,

00:01:15.218 --> 00:01:20.050
and add process or maintenance enrichment that made the hunt possible.

00:01:20.050 --> 00:01:24.443
Close each hunt with the result, confidence, affected assets, evidence,

00:01:24.443 --> 00:01:27.079
operational explanation, actions, and follow-up owner.

00:01:27.079 --> 00:01:32.350
Measure value through decisions and improvements, not the number of searches performed.

00:01:32.350 --> 00:01:38.500
A well-documented inconclusive hunt can still reveal exactly what visibility the program needs next.
